     `2^(7*L_3 + 10*L_4) * W_4 = 3^(10*L_2 + 7*L_3) * (W_2 - 1) + (3^(10*L_2 + 7*L_3) - 19 * Q_{L_3})`,
   since `0 < 19 * Q_{L_3} < 3^(10*L_2 + 7*L_3)` holds unconditionally for all `W_2, W_4 ∈ ℕ`,
   Euclidean division uniqueness yields:
